1
00:00:00,429 --> 00:00:01,629
Meet Oryn.

2
00:00:04,179 --> 00:00:06,299
The dual-pane file manager.

3
00:00:09,804 --> 00:00:12,494
Select your files. Drag them across.

4
00:00:17,304 --> 00:00:20,924
Browse in a grid, and preview images and Markdown in place.

5
00:00:22,929 --> 00:00:24,639
Or switch to columns.

6
00:00:24,804 --> 00:00:26,294
Filter as you type.

7
00:00:27,148 --> 00:00:29,898
Rename a whole batch, with a live preview.

8
00:00:31,835 --> 00:00:34,185
Open a zip like any other folder.

9
00:00:34,648 --> 00:00:37,410
Inside a repo, see exactly what changed.

10
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,850
Diff, blame and history, right beside your files.

11
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:44,040
And a terminal, already in the right folder.

12
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:47,254
Jump anywhere from the command palette.

13
00:00:47,304 --> 00:00:50,204
Even to your servers, over SFTP.

14
00:00:53,163 --> 00:00:54,519
On macOS.

15
00:00:54,569 --> 00:00:55,869
On Windows.

16
00:00:56,444 --> 00:00:57,804
And Linux.

17
00:01:02,772 --> 00:01:05,332
Oryn. Your files. In flow.

